{
  "source": "Prompts/people-skills-5.mp4",
  "duration": 168.693,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 2.76,
      "text": "Your group just finished this semester's history project."
    },
    {
      "start": 3.28,
      "end": 5.84,
      "text": "But Maya notices a problem with one of the examples"
    },
    {
      "start": 5.84,
      "end": 7.58,
      "text": "and starts suggesting a change."
    },
    {
      "start": 8.28,
      "end": 9.94,
      "text": "Before she can finish, someone interrupts."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.94,
      "end": 12.52,
      "text": "We are done, no more suggestions."
    },
    {
      "start": 13.6,
      "end": 16.82,
      "text": "Maya goes quiet, and the group moves on without addressing her point."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.5,
      "end": 19.96,
      "text": "You notice that Maya's expression and body language changed."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.8,
      "end": 21.4,
      "text": "She seems hurt."
    },
    {
      "start": 22.12,
      "end": 23.48,
      "text": "What would you say or do next?"
    },
    {
      "start": 24.22,
      "end": 26.46,
      "text": "Let's look at this board detailing your next move."
    },
    {
      "start": 27.02,
      "end": 29.5,
      "text": "Maya, we didn't hear the rest of your idea."
    },
    {
      "start": 30.12,
      "end": 30.64,
      "text": "Do you want to finish?"
    },
    {
      "start": 31.34,
      "end": 33.14,
      "text": "Maya actually has a valid point."
    },
    {
      "start": 33.66,
      "end": 36.46,
      "text": "The third example they included doesn't match the assignment's instructions."
    },
    {
      "start": 37.16,
      "end": 42.38,
      "text": "By giving her the floor again, the group now possesses the exact information they need to improve their work."
    },
    {
      "start": 42.98,
      "end": 46.54,
      "text": "Her idea deserves to be hurt, even if the group decides not to use it."
    },
    {
      "start": 47.16,
      "end": 49.64,
      "text": "What happened with Maya matters beyond this group project."
    },
    {
      "start": 50.2,
      "end": 53.98,
      "text": "That brings us to this graphic explaining why people's skills will matter more."
    },
    {
      "start": 53.98,
      "end": 55.92,
      "text": "First, you'll stand out."
    },
    {
      "start": 56.52,
      "end": 59.8,
      "text": "As more people use AI, polished work becomes an expectation."
    },
    {
      "start": 60.62,
      "end": 62.7,
      "text": "How you work with people helps you stand out."
    },
    {
      "start": 63.6,
      "end": 65.02,
      "text": "Second, trust still matters."
    },
    {
      "start": 65.74,
      "end": 70.08,
      "text": "People choose teammates and leaders who listen, keep promises, and treat others well."
    },
    {
      "start": 71.1,
      "end": 72.06,
      "text": "Finally, connection matters."
    },
    {
      "start": 72.68,
      "end": 73.88,
      "text": "AI can help with the work."
    },
    {
      "start": 74.46,
      "end": 77.44,
      "text": "People still need to feel heard, understood, and valued."
    },
    {
      "start": 78.18,
      "end": 80.3,
      "text": "Error-free output is rapidly becoming the baseline."
    },
    {
      "start": 80.3,
      "end": 88.24,
      "text": "The ability to navigate friction, validate contributions, and engage deeply with your team is the true professional differentiator."
    },
    {
      "start": 88.92,
      "end": 90.52,
      "text": "You can build these skills starting today."
    },
    {
      "start": 91.14,
      "end": 92.7,
      "text": "Let's walk through four ways to practice."
    },
    {
      "start": 93.7,
      "end": 94.88,
      "text": "Listen to understand."
    },
    {
      "start": 95.66,
      "end": 98.08,
      "text": "Do not plan your reply while the other person is talking."
    },
    {
      "start": 98.9,
      "end": 102.16,
      "text": "Ask one genuine follow-up question before offering your opinion."
    },
    {
      "start": 103.08,
      "end": 104.76,
      "text": "Notice what isn't being said."
    },
    {
      "start": 104.76,
      "end": 110.0,
      "text": "Pay attention to tone, hesitation, enthusiasm, and changes in behavior."
    },
    {
      "start": 110.8,
      "end": 113.12,
      "text": "If you're unsure what a change means, ask."
    },
    {
      "start": 114.04,
      "end": 115.12,
      "text": "Show people they matter."
    },
    {
      "start": 115.84,
      "end": 116.88,
      "text": "Remember what they tell you."
    },
    {
      "start": 117.3,
      "end": 121.06,
      "text": "Give specific appreciation and give people credit when an idea is theirs."
    },
    {
      "start": 121.98,
      "end": 122.8,
      "text": "Challenge ideas."
    },
    {
      "start": 123.56,
      "end": 123.84,
      "text": "Not people."
    },
    {
      "start": 124.72,
      "end": 126.6,
      "text": "Address difficult things directly and calmly."
    },
    {
      "start": 127.18,
      "end": 129.04,
      "text": "Explain the concern and suggest way forward."
    },
    {
      "start": 129.76,
      "end": 131.34,
      "text": "This example doesn't match the instructions."
    },
    {
      "start": 131.94,
      "end": 132.58,
      "text": "Could we try another?"
    },
    {
      "start": 132.58,
      "end": 142.16,
      "text": "These four habits take the abstract concept of empathy and translate it into a structured approach, keeping personal ego out of the workflow so collaboration can thrive."
    },
    {
      "start": 143.06,
      "end": 146.14,
      "text": "Returning to our history project, your intervention worked."
    },
    {
      "start": 146.88,
      "end": 148.6,
      "text": "The group fixes the problem Maya noticed."
    },
    {
      "start": 149.46,
      "end": 150.58,
      "text": "What could you say to give her credit?"
    },
    {
      "start": 151.66,
      "end": 156.86,
      "text": "In tomorrow's workplace, the systems you rely on will do the heavy lifting of drafting and organizing your data."
    },
    {
      "start": 157.78,
      "end": 158.56,
      "text": "AI can write it."
    },
    {
      "start": 158.98,
      "end": 160.54,
      "text": "It can't be the person in the room."
    },
    {
      "start": 160.54,
      "end": 165.24,
      "text": "Listen well, speak clearly, and be someone people want to work with."
    }
  ],
